  pamirs:{ en:'Pamirs (Congling)', zh:'帕米尔高原', names:['帕米尔高原','帕米尔','葱岭','Pamir Plateau','Pamirs','Pamir','Congling'], ll:[74.5, 38.5], kind:'mountain',
    era:{ en:'Called Congling (“Onion Ridge”) in ancient China', zh:'中国古代称葱岭' },
    info:{ en:'A knot of huge mountains where the Silk Road climbed over 4,000 m. China’s westernmost point is here.', zh:'帕米尔高原群山汇聚，丝绸之路要翻越海拔4000多米的山口。我国领土最西端就在这里。' },
    photos:[ { src:'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Karakul_lake_%281%29_%2831771493693%29.jpg/960px-Karakul_lake_%281%29_%2831771493693%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail', en:'Karakul Lake in the Pamirs', zh:'帕米尔高原的喀拉库勒湖', credit:'Hans Birger Nilsen', license:'CC BY-SA 2.0', page:'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karakul_lake_(1)_(31771493693).jpg' } ] },
